From 4293597616b34e502cb249057be173a88c27bf8b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 18:06:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 27/30] Typer: memoized witness scans; erroneous aliases are
 not signatures; self-check detail

The scans that ask whether a type mentions an assumed given or contains an
associated type are memoized per type, and rewriting is skipped where nothing
can change (premsubst made typing with long derivations slow).
sigrounds: a signature whose type is an alias of an erroneous type is not put
in the table.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011CH6tJP7hLkrpGFxEq7K6r
